# Antigravity Agent Rules - Blazor .NET 10 Portfolio

## Tech Stack Constraints
- Framework: Blazor WebAssembly Standalone targeting .NET 10 (`net10.0`).
- Language: C# 13+ with nullable reference types enabled.
- Database/Backend: `supabase-csharp` (Postgrest, Gotrue, Storage). Do NOT create an ASP.NET Core Web API backend; communicate directly with Supabase from WASM using Row-Level Security (RLS).
- Styling: Tailwind CSS. Never use Bootstrap or default Blazor purple gradients.

## Strict Color Palette & UI Theme
- Primary Background: `#05070B` (Obsidian Black)
- Card/Surface Background: `#0A0F1D` (Deep Navy) with `backdrop-blur-md`
- Elevated/Hover Surface: `#111A2E` (Midnight Navy)
- Primary Neon Accent: `#00F0FF` (Electric Cyan)
- Secondary Accent: `#2563EB` (Royal Blue)
- Text Primary: `#F8FAFC` (Slate 50)
- Text Secondary: `#94A3B8` (Slate 400)
- Borders: `border border-[#00F0FF]/20 hover:border-[#00F0FF]/60`
- Shadows on Hover: `hover:shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(0,240,255,0.2)]`
- Fonts: `Inter` for UI body/headings, `JetBrains Mono` for tags, metrics, and code.

## Coding Standards
- Always inherit `BaseModel` from `Supabase.Postgrest.Models` for database entities.
- Always convert uploaded images via `RequestImageFileAsync("image/webp", 1600, 900)` before uploading to the `portfolio-media` bucket.
- Never hardcode personal data in `.razor` files; always bind to `PortfolioDataService`.
- Gracefully handle offline or unconfigured Supabase credentials with fallback demo data so the app runs smoothly out-of-the-box.
